ull,null,null,null,null,9.2,null,9.1],"mta":[9.03,9.15,9.1,9.1,8.85,9.12,9.19,9.01,9,9.23],"notes":[null,null,null,null,null,"Tracker left out: too little of the month captured.","Tracker left out: too little of the month captured.",null,"Tracker left out: too little of the month captured.",null]},"metrics":[{"label":"Average speed, whole system","period":"July 2026","ours":"9.1 mph","mta":"9.2 mph","why":"Both averaged the same way: every route counts equally, every hour from 6 a.m. to midnight counts equally. The MTA's headline figure, which weights by miles driven, was 8.5 mph; long, slow local runs pull it down."},{"label":"Local routes, typical gap","period":"July 2026","ours":"9% faster","mta":"baseline","why":"Median across 261 local, limited and Select Bus Service routes. Likely cause: the tracker drops readings under 0.5 mph, so time spent stopped at stops and lights is left out, while the MTA counts it."},{"label":"Staten Island express (SIM)","period":"July 2026","ours":"10% slower","mta":"baseline","why":"Median across 27 SIM routes. This runs opposite to the local gap, and the cause is not yet known."},{"label":"Weekday riders","period":"July 2026","ours":"1.25M (MTA counters)","mta":"1.25M (MTA daily count)","why":"Both are MTA numbers. The first comes from passenger counters on board; the second is the MTA's daily bus ridership estimate. The riders chart above uses the counters."}],"flags":[{"head":"Routes line up almost exactly","text":"Rank the 338 routes both sources cover from slowest to fastest, and the two lists nearly match (rank correlation 0.99, where 1 is identical).","detail":"For comparing routes with each other, the tracker and the MTA tell the same story."},{"head":"Local buses read faster here","text":"On the typical local route the tracker reads 9% faster than the MTA. B41: 7.8 mph here, 6.5 MTA; M15+: 9.1 mph here, 7.9 MTA; BX19: 6.8 mph here, 5.6 MTA.","detail":"Treat the tracker's speed as speed while moving. The biggest gaps are on slow, crowded routes, where buses spend the most time stopped."},{"head":"Staten Island express buses read slower here","text":"The opposite happens on SIM express routes: the tracker reads them 10% slower. SIM22: 17.8 mph here, 23.9 MTA.","detail":"Not yet explained. Candidates include positions that refresh less often on highway stretches. The borough chart keeps express routes in their own group for this reason."},{"head":"Small monthly moves are noise here","text":"From May 2026 to July 2026 the tracker moved -0.1 mph and the MTA, averaged the same way, +0.2 mph.","detail":"Changes of a few tenths are within the tracker's noise: which late-evening hours the collector caught shifts from month to month."},{"head":"The MTA's two ridership counts disagree","text":"Over the last 12 months, the passenger-counter figure ran anywhere from 96% to 112% of the MTA's daily bus ridership count.","detail":"So a month-to-month change in riders depends on which count you use. Say which one."}],"numbers":{"routesPaired":338,"rankCorrelation":0.99,"localMedianRatio":1.087,"simMedianRatio":0.905,"mtaHeadline":{"2025-10":8.24,"2025-11":8.3,"2025-12":8.29,"2026-01":8.47,"2026-02":8.08,"2026-03":8.35,"2026-04":8.38,"2026-05":8.26,"2026-06":8.25,"2026-07":8.46},"mtaMatched":{"2025-10":9.03,"2025-11":9.15,"2025-12":9.1,"2026-01":9.1,"2026-02":8.85,"2026-03":9.12,"2026-04":9.19,"2026-05":9.01,"2026-06":9,"2026-07":9.23},"waitAssessment":{"2025-10":0.7018,"2025-11":0.7148,"2025-12":0.6929,"2026-01":0.74,"2026-02":0.6616,"2026-03":0.7092,"2026-04":0.7259,"2026-05":0.7065,"2026-06":0.6997,"2026-07":0.7274},"additionalBusStopTime":{"2025-10":2.57,"2025-11":2.52,"2025-12":2.8,"2026-01":2.14,"2026-02":3.87,"2026-03":2.59,"2026-04":2.25,"2026-05":2.67,"2026-06":2.68,"2026-07":2.23},"dailyRidershipWeekdayAvg":{"2025-10":1375163,"2025-11":1271489,"2025-12":1178246,"2026-01":1181308,"2026-02":1169491,"2026-03":1332753,"2026-04":1331258,"2026-05":1345860,"2026-06":1316866,"2026-07":1254897,"2026-